# The strongest champion this build holds: what an empty chair plays when a
# table is dealt without choosing. One generation, and the measurement that
# earned it the chair.
#
# Never inferred from the catalogue. Strength here is cyclic and runs number
# their own generations, so only the full profile can answer: head to head,
# against the anchor, solo against three heuristics, and against the known
# exploiter. A candidate takes this line by winning it; winning some axes
# earns a place on the roster instead, which is what trained-921 has.
#
# Profile a candidate against the STRONGEST ROSTER MEMBER, not against
# whoever holds this line. Reading only the incumbent is how 1905 took the
# chair in September while losing to 1798, which was sitting on the roster
# the whole time: 1798 had won some axes against 1159 and been given a
# roster place, and nothing ever put the two of them at the same table.
# A roster place is not a statement that the bot is weaker than this one.
#
# 1798 (neat-12), measured 2026-09-03 over 400 rounds a side, deep. It is
# the only champion that beats both of the others head to head:
#   vs trained-1905  -0.057 / -0.145   52.4% / 52.9%  (seeds 88 and 900,
#                    which do not overlap. Narrow, and the win intervals
#                    sit just clear of even, but it holds on both)
#   vs trained-1159  -0.212 / -0.239   57.9% / 59.1%  (seeds 88 and 900)
#   vs gen-642       -0.675            82.1%          (record. The
#                    exploiter plays flat, which is how every number on
#                    this axis has been taken and the only way they are
#                    comparable. 1905 reads -0.619 / 81.0%, overlapping)
#   vs anchor        -1.208            90.0%          (level with 1905's
#                    -1.187 / 90.5%, intervals overlapping heavily)
#
# The axis 1798 gives up, and it gives it up clearly: solo against three
# heuristics it reads -1.213 / 67.9% [65.5, 70.2] against 1905's -1.409 /
# 75.2% [73.0, 77.5], with the intervals disjoint on both measures. 1905
# is the better farmer of weak opposition. 1798 is the better player of
# strong opposition, and an empty chair at a table with a person in it is
# facing the second problem, not the first. That is the reading this line
# rests on, and it is a judgement rather than a sweep.
1798
